<h1>About</h1>

<p>Edmonton Cycle Club is a leisure cycling club based in Enfield, North London. While other clubs may
  concentrate on covering huge distances on-road, or negotiating mountainous terrain on MTBs, we're more
  into the sociable side of cycling. A ride with us tends to be mainly on towpaths, quiet country lanes and
  backstreets. Sometimes we head out into the surrounding Hertfordshire countryside, while other rides take
  us in towards London to discover a secret oasis of calm within the city.</p>

<p>Our regular rides vary in length: easier rides under 25 miles (suitable for families and less experienced
  riders) and longer, more challenging rides for the more experienced. The <a href="{{ '/diary/' | url }}">diary</a> gives
  details of each ride.</p>

<p>Club members often participate in cycling trips at home or abroad organised by third parties.</p>

<p>There's normally one or two rides every month (more in the summer, fewer in the winter), mostly on
  Sundays. Most rides start at 9:30 or 10am, and we generally stop for lunch at a pub or café and arrive back
  home between 4pm and 6pm. Check the <a href="{{ '/diary/' | url }}">diary</a> for details.</p>

<p>We also hold planning meetings and informal social evenings at the Winchmore Hill Sports Club every
  month.</p>

<p id="join">If all this sounds like your kind of thing, why not join us — membership is free!</p>

